Content shell: a page that asks to stay when its window closes, stays.

WebContents::DispatchBeforeUnload() runs a page's beforeunload handlers
before its tab closes, as a browser does, and the page may ask whether to
leave. WebContentsDelegate's default unloads the page and closes it
whatever the answer, and the shell kept the default: dismissing the
dialog closed the window all the same. The shell now goes on only when
the page may be left, as Chrome's browser does; zebkit_view_request_close()
(<zebkit/page.h>) relies on it.

--- a/content/shell/browser/shell.h
+++ b/content/shell/browser/shell.h
@@ -169,6 +169,11 @@
                           bool user_gesture,
                           bool last_unlocked_by_target) override;
   void CloseContents(WebContents* source) override;
+  // zebkit: a page kept by its beforeunload stays, rather than unloading
+  // all the same (the delegate's default).
+  void BeforeUnloadFired(WebContents* web_contents,
+                         bool proceed,
+                         bool* proceed_to_fire_unload) override;
   bool CanOverscrollContent() override;
   void NavigationStateChanged(WebContents* source,
                               InvalidateTypes changed_flags) override;
